---
import { PRODUCT_NAME } from '../../config';
import DocsLayout from '../../components/content/DocsLayout.astro';
import Kbd from '../../components/content/Kbd.astro';
import Shot from '../../components/content/Shot.astro';
import rewriteLight from '../../assets/features/rewrite-light.webp';
import rewriteDark from '../../assets/features/rewrite-dark.webp';
---
<DocsLayout title="Rewriting history" description={`Reword, squash, fixup, swap and delete commits in ${PRODUCT_NAME} with a single key, and undo any of it with ⌘Z.`}>
  <p>Select a commit on the map and press one key. {PRODUCT_NAME} rewrites the commit and replays every commit after it on the current branch for you. No editor and no todo list.</p>

  <h2 id="actions">The actions</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>Key</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Edit message</td><td><Kbd keys={['E']} /></td><td>Opens the full message for editing. Save to reword the commit.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Squash with parent</td><td><Kbd keys={['S']} /></td><td>Combines the commit with its parent and keeps both messages.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fixup with parent</td><td><Kbd keys={['F']} /></td><td>Combines the commit with its parent and keeps only the parent's message.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Swap with parent</td><td>••• menu</td><td>Swaps the order of the commit and its parent.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Delete commit</td><td><Kbd keys={['⌫']} /></td><td>Removes the commit's changes from the branch.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <Shot light={rewriteLight} dark={rewriteDark} alt="The commit menu with its Rewrite section: Edit Message, Squash, Fixup, Swap with Parent and Delete Commit" />

  <h2 id="moving">Moving commits between branches</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Rebase the current branch onto the selected commit</td><td><Kbd keys={['R']} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Merge the selected commit into the current branch</td><td><Kbd keys={['M']} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cherry-pick the selected commit onto the current branch</td><td><Kbd keys={['P']} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Revert the selected commit</td><td><Kbd keys={['V']} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>To point the current branch at another commit, choose <strong>Move “branch” here</strong> in the commit's ••• menu.</p>

  <h2 id="undo">If you change your mind</h2>
  <p>Every rewrite is one step on the undo stack. <Kbd keys={['⌘', 'Z']} /> puts the branch back exactly as it was, and <Kbd keys={['⇧', '⌘', 'Z']} /> does it again. See <a href="/docs/undo-redo">Undo and redo</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The commit has to be on the <strong>current branch</strong>. To rewrite a commit on another branch, check that branch out first.</li>
    <li><strong>Merge commits</strong> can't be rewritten, and neither can history that has a merge between the commit and HEAD, because replaying it would flatten the merge.</li>
    <li>Squash, fixup and swap need a parent, so they don't apply to the first commit in the repository.</li>
    <li>Uncommitted changes are set aside during the rewrite and put back afterwards.</li>
    <li>Rewriting commits you have already pushed means the next push has to be a force push. {PRODUCT_NAME} asks before force pushing, and uses <code>--force-with-lease</code> so it won't overwrite someone else's new work.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
